# Feature Addition Template

Standard path for new performance-safe overlay features. Follow this checklist before merging.

## Data sources (required)

- Use **`GameContextSnapshot`** for chain resolution — never call `TryResolve` on hot paths.
- Use **`UiContextSnapshot`** for GameUi / controller branches — never assemble branch order in feature code.
- Use **`UiProjector.TryRect`** for UI element screen rects.
- Use **`PanelCatalogSnapshot`** for open-window detection (Ritual, runeforge, map panels).
- Use **`EntityContextSnapshot`** / **`WorldSnapshot`** for entity lists — component-map walks stay in **`Poe2Live.ResolveComponent`** only.
- Use **`InputActionCatalog`** for any user-triggered bind — one catalog entry, not edits across ImGui/API/dashboard.

## Cadence

- Give memory/UI work its own `PerformanceCadence` or reuse an existing Hz setting.
- Never piggyback entity walks or UI BFS on `FpsCap` / render rate.

## Performance

- Add **`FeaturePerfAccumulator`** timing for any new memory/UI prep category.
- Keep fallback scans throttled and opt-in — steady-state counters must stay flat.
- No memory reads on the ImGui render thread.

## Settings & input

- Add **`SettingHints.*`** for every user-facing control.
- Wire ImGui tooltip + dashboard `title=` from the same hint.
- Register bindable actions in **`InputActionCatalog`**; verify keyboard + gamepad display in tests.

## Threading

- One writer per mutable store; publish immutable snapshots for readers.
- Marshal UI actions through `_commandQueue` onto the main tick thread.

## Tests & verification

- Unit test pure logic (catalog, snapshots, migration).
- `dotnet test -c Release` before merge.
- Compare `FeaturePerfSnapshot` before/after when touching hot paths.

## Probe (optional)

- Add a Research probe only when live validation requires in-game state.
